    "introduction": "M&G provides savings, investment and retirement products to individuals and institutions. Its asset-management operations run portfolios across public and private markets, while its life and savings business serves policyholders through pensions, annuities and other long-term products. Revenue includes investment-management fees and income associated with managing insurance and savings contracts. The businesses connect customer assets with investment capabilities, but have different capital requirements and cash-flow patterns. Performance depends on investment outcomes, customer inflows and withdrawals, market conditions and the cost of administering policies. Managing long-term commitments alongside new business is an important part of maintaining customer relationships and financial resilience.",
